   "source": [
    "## Parameter estimation\n",
    "Takes real S&P data and estimates mu and sigma using maximum lieklyhood estimation"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 52,
   "id": "2fa03c2f-358c-4226-af3a-ce536f5c3888",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "from scipy import stats\n",
    "import yfinance as yf"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b63badac-2472-4c79-ad8f-d246b963d178",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "collects data"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 53,
   "id": "e4b2bdb1-b837-47c7-bd00-e4a4732f1c9b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stderr",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "[*********************100%***********************]  1 of 1 completed"
     ]
    },
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Downloaded 1006 days of SPY data\n",
      "From : 2020-01-02\n",
      "To   : 2023-12-29\n",
      "Start price : $296.13\n",
      "End price   : $461.39\n"
     ]
    },
    {
     "name": "stderr",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "ticker = \"SPY\"\n",
    "data   = yf.download(ticker, start=\"2020-01-01\", end=\"2024-01-01\")\n",
    "prices = data[\"Close\"] # takes only closing price\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Downloaded {len(prices)} days of {ticker} data\")\n",
    "print(f\"From : {prices.index[0].date()}\")\n",
    "print(f\"To   : {prices.index[-1].date()}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Start price : ${prices.iloc[0].item():.2f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"End price   : ${prices.iloc[-1].item():.2f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "bd45b777-16a2-4089-a91c-dc96694e11b5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "calculates log return"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 54,
   "id": "03f9b451-812c-4114-880b-e8bcbe6d99db",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Number of log returns : 1005\n",
      "Mean daily log return : 0.000441\n",
      "Std  daily log return : 0.014315\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "log_returns = np.log(prices / prices.shift(1)).dropna() # log return of each trading day (close-to-close)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Number of log returns : {len(log_returns)}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Mean daily log return : {log_returns.mean().item():.6f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Std  daily log return : {log_returns.std().item():.6f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "bcd69ee1-a61a-4275-826f-f0f7a06a61d9",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "carries out MLE on daily data"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 55,
   "id": "005e92fe-5b6d-46da-9704-276b54b920b4",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "mu_daily    = log_returns.mean().item() # daily log-return drift\n",
    "sigma_daily = log_returns.std().item() # daily log-return volitility"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7a074f40-b565-4df9-b320-351c0b992630",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "anualises estimates using log-return distribution"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 56,
   "id": "96ed285f-76a1-48f9-bb31-04d928af6b2b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Parameter                 Value\n",
      "annual drift             0.1370\n",
      "annual volitility        0.2272\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "sigma_hat = sigma_daily * np.sqrt(252) # measured variance is sigma^2 * delta_t (1/252). rearrange to get annual std estime\n",
    "mu_hat    = mu_daily * 252 + 0.5 * sigma_hat**2  # measured mu is (mu- 1/2 *sigma^2) * delta_t. rearrange to get annual mu estimate\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"{'Parameter':20} {'Value':>10}\")\n",
    "print(f\"{'annual drift':20} {mu_hat:>10.4f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"{'annual volitility':20} {sigma_hat:>10.4f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e5d78f8d-bac2-466f-a2b4-b26164b7383a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Simulation"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 57,
   "id": "896c0c16-4e5b-4655-a765-84ee2ad0a070",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from utils import gbm_simulate"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "274a8f07-140c-4234-97db-7001f13b4b96",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Parameters"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 58,
   "id": "d66a0d26-922f-4429-9915-d695645c0cd8",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "S0 = prices.iloc[0].item()\n",
    "N = len(prices) - 1\n",
    "T = N/252\n",
    "I = 50"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6d353c82-c252-4365-9031-b01385175cdf",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Run simulation"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 59,
   "id": "3b1e97e7-2d00-4509-9e52-be75bdcbb95a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Starting price   : $296.13\n",
      "Mean final price : $481.66\n",
      "Min  final price : $140.57\n",
      "Max  final price : $1073.36\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "S, times = gbm_simulate(S0, mu_hat, sigma_hat, T, N, I)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Starting price   : ${S[0, 0]:.2f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Mean final price : ${S[-1].mean():.2f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Min  final price : ${S[-1].min():.2f}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Max  final price : ${S[-1].max():.2f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8841e7aa-9b55-4082-91bb-65db40fd5ba3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Plot simulations against SPY"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 60,
   "id": "0fbab757-327d-4177-9f27-1dff7f14778e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1200x500 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "plt.figure(figsize=(12,5))\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.plot(times, S, alpha=0.6, color = \"g\") # simulated paths\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.plot(times, prices, lw=2, color = \"r\", label=\"SPY data\") # real data\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.plot(times, S.mean(axis=1), lw=2, color='k', \n",
    "         linestyle='--', label='Mean Simulated Path') # average of simaltions\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.title(\"GBM Simulated vs SPY data\")\n",
    "plt.xlabel(\"Time (Years)\")\n",
    "plt.ylabel(\"Price ($)\")\n",
    "plt.legend()\n",
    "plt.show()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "588a820e-b65a-4b38-8200-29c5dea4df09",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Evaluation"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f3d18c8b-9aae-44eb-bbd5-9ca31b702bd9",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Mean value of simulations follows real data well, suggesting our drift estimate is realtively accurate. However, the simulated paths have a evry large spread. This shows that our method of modelling volitility needs improvement. The cause of this is one of the main limitations of GBM as a model, it assumes a constant  value for volitility over time. In realisty this is not the case.\n",
    "\n",
    "One example of this is the 2020 market crash due to covid which can be seen near the beginning of our dataset. Volitlility spiked in thsi period and took time to return to normal levels. This is an example of volitility clustering.\n",
    "\n",
    "To model for this behavour, we can estimate the current volitility on a rolling basis, using recent price data."
   ]
  },
